ic for `EsRelation` has been removed from the `apply` method. This could lead to synthetic attributes not being filtered out as intended. Ensure that this functionality is still covered elsewhere in the codebase, possibly by integrating it into another part of the transformation process.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-62592:62943-60654:60738","promptId":"#E7TTX","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":62592,"endPos":62943,"startLine":1249,"startLineOffset":93,"endLine":1255,"endLineOffset":13,"length":352}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":60654,"endPos":60738,"startLine":1217,"startLineOffset":21,"endLine":1217,"endLineOffset":105,"length":85}]}]},{"comment":"The change introduces a new condition to check if both `groupings` and `aggregates` are resolved using `Resolvables.resolved()`. However, the original logic checked if all expressions were resolved by calling `stats.expressionsResolved()`, which is now removed. This could lead to incorrect behavior if there are other expressions in `Stats` that need resolution beyond just `groupings` and `aggregates`.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-22539:22575,22595:22607,22608:22618,22635:22647,22848:22873,23000:23034-22413:22516,22536:22545,22546:22555,22572:22581,22782:22801,22928:22936","promptId":"#0X6BJ","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":22539,"endPos":22575,"startLine":461,"st